THE BASEL PROBLEM
Sum of reciprocals of squares

    ∞
    ∑  1/n²  =  π² / 6
   n=1

TYPES & VARIABLES
  n     : positive integer          n ∈ ℕ = {1, 2, 3, …}
  s     : complex variable          s ∈ ℂ
  ζ(s)  : Riemann zeta function     ζ(s) = ∑ 1/n^s   (Re(s) > 1)
  π     : circle constant           π ≈ 3.14159…
  i     : imaginary unit            i² = −1
  x     : real angle                x ∈ ℝ

FUNDAMENTALS
  ζ(2) = π²/6

  Euler’s formula (unit circle):
      e^{ix} = cos x + i sin x
      |e^{ix}| = 1

  Infinite product for sine:
      sin x = x  ∏ (1 − x²/(n² π²))
               n=1

  Expanding the product and matching
  coefficients of x³ forces the series
  ∑ 1/n² to equal π²/6.

HISTORY
  Solved by Leonhard Euler, 1734
  (Basel problem, posed 1644)
